# {{PROJECT_NAME}} development rules

This independent repository owns {{PROJECT_NAME}}.
<!-- 待定制：在此补一句英文产品描述：它是什么、给谁用、由哪些部分组成（例如 LoomlineRetopo：半自动的游戏低模服装拓扑工具；MtoULiveLink：Maya 组件加 Unreal 插件的实时联动；StoUTextureSync：Painter 到 Unreal 的贴图同步插件） -->
It can be cloned alone and may be mounted as a registered submodule in a
collection repository, which owns only the registration and the pinned commit.
Run Git and `gh` here for product work and do not change sibling projects.

## Read first

Read an existing `HANDOFF.md` first and reconcile it with Git (see Session
handoff). The other project documents are written in Chinese because the user
reviews them. Read the ones your task needs, not all of them. Read a document
you open in full: they are short, and a constraint missed in a skipped section
costs more than the reading.

Every task reads:

- [CONTEXT.md](CONTEXT.md): vocabulary. Use these terms and code names
  exactly.
- The task's own entry in [docs/roadmap.md](docs/roadmap.md) (`S<stage>-T<n>`
  IDs): its scope and completion criteria. Read the rest of the roadmap only
  when planning or reordering work.

Then read by what the task touches:

| The task touches | Read |
| --- | --- |
| Modules, data objects, commands, dependencies, layout | [docs/architecture.md](docs/architecture.md) |
| What the product does or does not do (`G-`, `F-`, `NG-`, `Q-` IDs) | [docs/requirements.md](docs/requirements.md) |
| Delivering, reviewing, experiments, visual acceptance, architecture changes, releases | [docs/workflow.md](docs/workflow.md) |
| The rationale of a decision in force | The linked entry in `docs/adr/` ([README](docs/adr/README.md)) |

