When unsure whether a document applies, read it. A reviewer reads every
document the change under review falls under.

These rules apply to every contributor and tool. Stay within the scope you
were given. Something those documents forbid is not worked around: raise it as
docs/workflow.md section 8 describes. Something they simply do not cover is an
ordinary implementation choice and is yours to make.

## Working with the user

- The user is a 3D game artist who does not write code. Contributors own
  algorithm design, code and technical route; the user owns product
  direction, project-specific conventions, usage feedback and every
  outward-facing decision. docs/workflow.md section 2 lists what must go to
  the user and what must not.
- Talk to the user in Chinese, in art-pipeline terms. Do not hand them code,
  commands to type, or a technical choice to make.
- The user's comments are evidence to reason about, not rules by decree: if one
  conflicts with the principles of the problem or common practice, say so and
  discuss it. When you give the user something to look at, look at it yourself
  first.
